 FlatNest Mobile API — Implementation Guide

 Why owner side first?

 Yes — owner side first is the right call. Here's why:
 - Renters browse listings → listings must exist first
 - Auth is shared (both need it), so you build it once
 - The 4-step listing wizard is the most complex flow — get it done while fresh
 - After owner is done, renter side is mostly read-only and much simpler

 ---
 Implementation Order

 Phase 1 → Auth (shared)
 Phase 2 → Owner: complete registration + listing wizard + dashboard
 Phase 3 → Renter: feed + detail + wishlist
 Phase 4 → Chat (works for both sides)
 Phase 5 → Notifications
 Phase 6 → Reference data (geo + amenities — use on forms)

 ---
 Setup

 Base URL

 http://localhost:8000/api/v1

 Headers (every request)

 Content-Type: application/json
 Accept: application/json

 Auth header (protected routes only)

 Authorization: Bearer {access_token}

 Error format (all errors follow this shape)

 { "message": "Human readable text", "code": "MACHINE_CODE" }

 Common error codes

 ┌───────────────────────┬──────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────┐
 │         Code          │ HTTP │                   Meaning                    │
 ├───────────────────────┼──────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────┤
 │ INVALID_CREDENTIALS   │ 401  │ Wrong email/password                         │
 ├───────────────────────┼──────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────┤
 │ INVALID_REFRESH_TOKEN │ 401  │ Refresh token expired/invalid                │
 ├───────────────────────┼──────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────┤
 │ NOT_FOUND             │ 404  │ Resource doesn't exist                       │
 ├───────────────────────┼──────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────┤
 │ FORBIDDEN             │ 403  │ Not your resource                            │
 ├───────────────────────┼──────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────┤
 │ INCOMPLETE            │ 422  │ Listing missing area or photos before submit │
 └───────────────────────┴──────┴──────────────────────────────────────────────┘

 Validation errors (422)

 {
   "message": "The given data was invalid.",
   "errors": {
     "email": ["The email has already been taken."]
   }
 }

 ---
 Phase 1 — Auth (build this first, shared by both sides)

 Step 1 of 3 — Register

 POST /auth/register
 Content-Type: application/json
 Body:
 {
   "name": "string, required, max 100",
   "email": "string, required, unique",
   "password": "string, required, min 8",
   "phone": "string, required, BD format 01XXXXXXXXX, unique"
 }
 Response 201:
 {
   "access_token": "string",
   "refresh_token": "string",
   "registration_step": 2,
   "user": {
     "id": "uuid",
     "name": "string",
     "email": "string",
     "phone": "string",
     "role": "renter",
     "avatar_url": null,
     "is_complete": false
   }
 }

 ▎ Save access_token and refresh_token after this. User is logged in.

 ---
 Step 2 of 3 — Save role + date of birth

 PATCH /auth/register/details
 Authorization: Bearer {token}
 Content-Type: application/json
 Body:
 {
   "role": "renter | owner",
   "date_of_birth": "YYYY-MM-DD (must be 18+)"
 }
 Response 200:
 { "message": "Details saved", "registration_step": 3 }

 ▎ If user selects owner, they will later see the listing creation flow.

 ---
 Step 3 of 3 — Upload avatar

 PATCH /auth/register/avatar
 Authorization: Bearer {token}
 Content-Type: multipart/form-data
 Body:
 avatar: file (jpg/jpeg/png, max 2MB)
 Response 200:
 { "message": "Registration complete", "avatar_url": "https://..." }

 ▎ is_complete becomes true. Redirect to home screen.

