 ---
 Start a new chat (renter initiates)

 POST /chats
 Authorization: Bearer {token}
 Content-Type: application/json
 Body:
 {
   "listing_id": "uuid",
   "initial_message": "Hi, is this flat still available?"
 }
 Response 201:
 { "chat_id": "uuid" }

 ▎ If a chat for this listing already exists between these users, the existing chat is returned.

 ---
 Load messages in a chat

 GET /chats/{id}/messages
 Authorization: Bearer {token}
 Automatically marks all messages in this chat as read.

 Response 200:
 {
   "chat": { "id": "uuid" },
   "messages": [
     {
       "id": "uuid",
       "chat_id": "uuid",
       "sender_id": "uuid",
       "sender": { "id": "uuid", "name": "string", "avatar_url": "string | null" },
       "text": "string",
       "is_read": true,
       "created_at": "ISO datetime"
     }
   ]
 }

 ---
 Send a message

 POST /chats/{id}/messages
 Authorization: Bearer {token}
 Content-Type: application/json
 Body:
 { "text": "Yes it's available, come visit!" }
 Response 201: Single message object (same shape as message in list above)

 ▎ This fires a Pusher event on channel private-chat.{chat_id} with event message.sent.
 ▎ The receiver also gets a notification (kind = message).

 ---
 Real-time (Pusher) — subscribe to a chat

 Channel : private-chat.{chat_id}
 Event   : message.sent
 Payload : MessageResource (same shape as message above)

